 The pages under `docs/` are this repository's source of truth for people and coding agents. This page says which page
 owns each fact; read it before writing one.
+
+## Kinds
+
+- [Philosophy](philosophy.md) owns the standing trade-offs that guide new proposals (explanation). Its single page
+  has a lead and `Tenets`; each tenet states what it rules out and links the decision records that apply it.
+- [Architecture](architecture.md) owns the system's parts and how they connect (explanation). Its single page has a
+  lead, `Parts` and `How they connect`; reasons for choices live in the linked decision records.
+- [Decisions](adrs/README.md) own the reasons for foundation choices whose reversal changes more than one feature
+  or module (explanation). Each `NNNN-<slug>.md` has a lead, `Context`, `Options`, `Decision` and `Consequences`.
+  Implementation choices below that bar stay in code and review; standing trade-offs belong in Philosophy.
+- [Features](features/README.md) own member-visible behavior (explanation). Each page has a lead, sections describing
+  the behavior and its limits, and links to the decisions that shaped it.
+- [Runbooks](runbooks/README.md) own responses to operational triggers (how-to). Each page has a lead naming the
+  trigger and owner, `Before you begin`, `Steps` with expected results, and `If it fails`.
+
+[Glossary](glossary.md) owns shared terminology: each entry names the concept, defines it and lists rejected
+synonyms under `Avoid`. State a fact on its owning page and link to it elsewhere.
